{"id":"5d30cf84-6bde-4c96-af7a-0a79c45da5ba","createdAt":"2026-10-05 15:49 +02:00","priority":"Low","status":"Done","description":"PPTFeatureStatus usage audit: Questions/Wished/Backlog are non-active Open states; Wished is the create default. Queued is set by Start, adds the feature JSON to DEVENVOPDEV.md, stays in .features, and appears alongside Committed on the Queued tab; Committed is set after a successful Git commit and removes its task marker. InProgress, Delivered, and Backlog have no dedicated transition side effects beyond status updates; Backlog is the legacy default. Done stamps deliveredDate, removes a task marker, and Done records in .current migrate to .features on refresh/commit. Aborted removes the task marker but keeps the record in .features. Denied moves the record to .archived and removes other copies. Archived moves the record to .archived; archived-list reads normalize records to Archived except Denied. Questions: Should Queued mean actively worked on and Committed mean ready to pick up? Should starting move the same feature ID from .features into .current, and should DEVENVOPDEV.md be a separate task list or a view of those active features? What should InProgress represent? Are Delivered and Done distinct? Which statuses should users be allowed to select, and which transitions should be automatic?","deliveredDate":"2026-10-05"}
{"id":"1b89a6de-143f-4335-9801-c98df764e1b8","createdAt":"2026-10-05 15:51 +02:00","priority":"Low","status":"Done","description":"Remaining PPTFeature system inventory: shared PPTFeature/PPTFeatureStatus/FeaturePriority types; Angular feature page at /feature with add, open/queued/done/archived lists, status and priority editing, descriptions, ordering, start/done/deny/abort/archive actions and filtering; backlog and state-reference views; backend client for feature CRUD/order/status/archive APIs; Express routes for /features, /backlog, /archived and per-feature operations. Server persists JSON-lines to .features and .archived, accepts legacy .wishlist/.backlog/.delivered stores and converts older text records, tracks active work in DEVENVOPDEV.md and .current, migrates Done records on refresh/commit, and moves Denied/Archived records to the archive store. Git commit marks the active feature Committed; client FeatureWorkService and CurrentTaskService keep active feature/task state and toolbar display in sync. Tests cover client, API, migration, archival and commit behavior. Open questions: which capabilities and stores are intended to survive the planned reset, whether task and feature are separate concepts, what Queued versus Committed should mean, and whether the feature API/types/commit integration should be removed along with the UI.","deliveredDate":"2026-10-05"}
